# Review standard for the extension (internal-review-repo#4)

Judged against the `Research objective` internal-review-repo#4, on top of R1-R4 in
`review/standard.md`, which the delivered results must still meet unchanged.
Baseline: the released delivery, `paper-repo` 7f8c5f7a5f08ad84c2746a9d559d724547c1d0e8.

## E1 Quadratic fit
- Same 40 points as R1 (x = 0..39, `default_rng(227)`, `rng.normal(0, 3, 40)`), not redrawn
  differently; OLS on [1, x, x^2], 95% t-intervals with df = 37 (t = 2.0262), SEs from the
  residual variance; method stated.
- Independent reference (numpy 2.4.6, scipy 1.17.1):
  a = 4.97158 [2.39471, 7.54844]; b = 0.58626 [0.28057, 0.89195];
  c = 0.0041569 [-0.00342, 0.01173]; RSS = 293.470 (line: 303.272).
  Reported values must agree to the stated precision, or the difference must be explained.
- Statements about the true values (2.5, 0.8, 0) relative to the intervals are correct if made
  (c's interval contains 0).

## E2 AIC comparison
- Gaussian maximum-likelihood AIC for both models on the same 40 points, the convention
  stated (with or without the sigma parameter, constant terms or not; the difference is the
  same either way): delta AIC (quadratic - line) = +0.686. With sigma counted:
  AIC line 200.545, quadratic 201.231 (n ln(RSS/n) + 2p form: 85.030 / 85.716).
- Conclusion matches the numbers: the line has the lower AIC, but by < 2, so the data do not
  meaningfully distinguish them / give no support for the curvature. "By how much" is stated
  quantitatively (delta AIC; optionally Akaike weights ~0.58/0.42, AICc delta 1.16, or the
  nested F-test p = 0.27 as corroboration). Overclaiming ("strongly prefers the line") or
  claiming support for the quadratic is a finding.

## E3 Figure
- The existing figure keeps the data points and the fitted line and adds the quadratic curve,
  distinguishable from the line (style/colour) and identified in the legend or caption; axes
  labelled; readable; embedded in the report, link resolves in the assembled delivery; any
  annotated numbers match E1. Opened and inspected, not only its provenance.

## E4 Report and code
- `report/report.md` extended, still about one page; the line-fit and pi results are kept as
  delivered (numbers identical to the release); pi simulation not rerun (results.json and
  log unchanged from the release).
- New numbers (a, b, c, CIs, AIC values, delta) traceable to delivered code and output files
  next to the report; the code runs as given and reproduces them; versions recorded.
